- Mutual Termination Rights. Either party may, in addition to any other remedies available to it under this Agreement or at law or in equity, terminate this Agreement (or, in the event this Agreement has been previously terminated, the Wind Down Period, if any) immediately upon the issuance of written notice to the other party in the event that:  
- (i) the other party materially breaches a material provision of this Agreement, and fails to cure such breach within thirty (30) days;  
- (ii) the other party undergoes an Insolvency Event.

- Yes, a party may terminate this Agreement immediately through written notice if certain conditions are met.
  - (i) the other party ceases to carry on business as a going concern;
  - (ii) the other party becomes or may become the object of the institution of voluntary or involuntary proceedings in bankruptcy or liquidation; 
  - (iii) a receiver or similar officer is appointed with respect to the whole or a substantial part of the other party's assets; 
  - (iv) an event similar to any of the foregoing occurs under applicable law.

- Can a party terminate this contract without cause? 
- Yes, the Consultant can terminate the Agreement and the Term automatically if:
  1. The five-year Term expires on January 31, 2025;
  2. The Consultant should no longer be able to provide the Services through the Principal for any reason;
